[Music]  tracking down and prosecuting the  estimated 2 000 suspects involved in the  january 6 attack has turned in one of  the biggest investigations in the  history of the fbi so far more than 700  people are facing criminal charges after  investigators scoured tens of thousands  of hours of video evidence but the  professionals could not do all of that  alone in fact they relied on help from  the public and that includes an  interesting group of amateur detectives  our jefferson spoke with members of this  group they're secretive understandably  they're worried about threats themselves  jeff good morning what do you know good  morning tony the so-called sedition  hunters are amateur detectives who come  from all walks of life a teacher who  squeezed in research between classes a  union worker even a grandmother but they  all have one thing in common the horror  that they felt on january 6.  that day is seared in so many minds  mobs of rioters  pummeling and beating police officers  and trying to breach capital doors  i was watching all these people hurt  officers desecrate congress and no one  was getting arrested what this woman saw  on january 6 motivated her to do  something we aren't identifying her  because like others working to identify  rioters she's concerned about her safety  what happened means something to you  well a democracy is only as healthy as  its citizenry in a democracy its  citizens have to care  they have to care about the rule of law  reading through tens of thousands of  images produced that day this  politically independent grandmother  joined the crowdsource collaborative  movement of sedition hunters almost  immediately was there one in particular  that sickened you caveman who beat  officer miller with the with the flag  pretty much anyone in the tunnel that  day  participated in mass mob violence john  scott railton was also closely watching  the attack one image stopped me in my  tracks and that was a picture of a man  wearing body armor holding a clutch of  temporary restraints in the visitor's  chamber of the senate i thought my god  what is going on in the capital of my  country railton an internet researcher  focused on hacking and disinformation  got to work trying to identify the  masked man looking at the image what is  this guy wearing what's he carrying how  does he move  and through that process which would be  called open source investigation  ultimately we got to an identity railton  motivated others to start sifting  through the mountains of evidence  available on tv and social media people  began joining groups and collaborating  with each other that ultimately led to  some really remarkable discoveries and  successes to me it sounds like finding a  needle in a haystack  it's like finding a needle in a haystack  of needles some of this addition hunters  would work with images just focused on  tracking people in the crowds others  focused on building timelines or  geo-locating individuals on maps of the  capital it's like looking at a picture  what's in the background where do i  think the person taking this video was  standing what else in that video  corresponds to a time period that i  already know they even established  ethical guidelines of what not to do for  example they don't name individuals  before an arrest has been made  the group's findings including nicknames  they gave to rioters have ended up in  charging documents and fbi case agents  continue to ask for the public's help  any assistance in this kind of  assistance is really vital former fbi  agent catherine schweitz says the  sedition hunter's work has undoubtedly  led to faster results it is by far the  largest number of people that the fbi  has ever had to investigate the fact  that the citizens are stepping up is  taking the time period and shrinking it  down substantially still there remain  more than 250 people wanted by the fbi  for allegedly assaulting federal  officers and ultimately the number of  arrests could more than double you know  that old saying many hands will make  light work with the help of the sedition  hunters grandma's got new hobbies she's  got gardening hobby in the spring summer  and fall and sedition hunting  hobby in the winter time if i a simple  little old gray-haired grandma  can do this anyone can  the people we spoke with believe that  there are hundreds if not thousands of  people doing this kind of work and  they've gathered tony this  massive database 1800 images and even  names  of some of the people that they've been  able been able to track down and it's a  huge amount of work for law enforcement  i know this investigation could go on  for years to come they could still be  tracking people down bringing charges  but before we look into the future i'm  interested in the past you were here on  january 6th what are your memories of  that day  i will never forget how all of it  started i was at the ellipse where the  rally was and as soon as rudy giuliani  took the stage and said trial buy combat  and then the president took the stage  you could see the the tone in the crowd  changing they came this way in fact  there was a man beating on our cbs news  truck and he looked like he wanted to  hurt us  but once we were able to get out of the  truck we came up here and then of course  i saw people climbing the walls  harrowing memories of 365 days ago jeff  thank you very much

